<title>DENMARK: Danish Oct trade surplus 2.123 billion DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish Oct trade surplus 2.123 billion DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark posted a trade surplus excluding ships of 2.123 billion crowns in October 1996 compared to a revised 2.940 billion crowns surplus in September 1996, the national statistics office said on Friday.  </p>
<p>DANISH TRADE (billions of crowns):</p>
<p>			     Oct 1996     Sept 1996   Oct 1995</p>
<p> Exports		     25.744	  24.569     24.588</p>
<p> Imports		     23.977	  21.677     22.297</p>
<p> Trade balance		1.766	   2.892	2.291</p>
<p> Trade balance excl ships 2.123	   2.940	2.098</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted balance excluding ships</p>
<p>				  2.309	   1.765	2.109</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast an average October trade surplus excluding ships of 2.2 billion crowns. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
